From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:36:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] connectivity: leave restricted networks without allowed UID
 ranges

The LineageOS firewall installs, on every network, the UID ranges that its
transport policy allows. A network without NET_CAPABILITY_NOT_RESTRICTED has
no disallowed UIDs, because it chooses its own allowed UIDs, and the range list
built from an empty denylist is the single range from 0 to Integer.MAX_VALUE.
Netd lets a UID use a physical network when a range includes it, whatever its
permission bits, so any app could bind a socket to a restricted network.

A restricted network now gets no ranges, as on AOSP. updateAllowedUidsForNetwork
skips the add for an empty configuration and still removes the previous one,
so a network that becomes restricted loses its old range.
---
 service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java b/service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java
index 7682d5082635aeaa6f36c555c51f0ab2c17932c6..f584e5d0ac9b8270055394963c81fcfb33032eaa 100644
--- a/service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java
+++ b/service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java
@@ -955,10 +955,17 @@ public class ConnectivityService extends IConnectivityManager.Stub
 
     /**
      * Returns an array of UidRangeParcel representing all possible UIDs that are not restricted
-     * by policy, based on the provided network and its capabilities.
+     * by policy, based on the provided network and its capabilities. A restricted network has
+     * none: it chooses its own allowed UIDs.
      */
     private UidRangeParcel[] getUidRangeParcelsAllowedByPolicyForNetwork(
             @NonNull final NetworkAgentInfo nai) {
+        if (!nai.networkCapabilities.hasCapability(NET_CAPABILITY_NOT_RESTRICTED)) {
+            // Netd lets a UID use a physical network that has a range including the UID, whatever
+            // its permission bits. Nothing is disallowed on a restricted network, so the ranges
+            // below would be the single range of every UID and any app could bind to the network.
+            return new UidRangeParcel[0];
+        }
         final var uids = getUidsDisallowedByPolicyForNetwork(nai);
         final var ranges = new ArrayList<UidRangeParcel>();
         int lastUid = 0;
